# Firebase CLI deploy cache
.firebase/

# Service-account keys. This repo is PUBLIC, and a downloaded key is a live credential with
# deploy rights to the Firebase project: committing one hands anybody who reads GitHub the
# ability to publish to the site. These patterns cover what the Google Cloud console and the
# Firebase CLI actually name their downloads, so a key dropped in here by accident is ignored
# rather than staged. The key belongs in the GitHub secret FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT and
# nowhere else on disk; delete the file once it is set. See FIREBASE.md.
*-service-account*.json
*serviceaccount*.json
*-adminsdk-*.json
firebase-adminsdk*.json
gha-creds-*.json
